\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Gives the probability of transition from any state to any other.
 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mathbf{P}=\left[\begin{array}{ccccc}
P_{00} & \cdots & P_{i0} & \cdots & P_{N0}\\
\vdots & \ddots &  &  & \vdots\\
P_{0j} &  & P_{ij} &  & P_{Nj}\\
\vdots &  &  & \ddots & \vdots\\
P_{0N} & \cdots & P_{iN} & \cdots & P_{NN}\end{array}\right].\]

\end_inset

where probability of transition from state 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 to state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset

 is given by 
\begin_inset Formula $P_{ij}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout ShortFoilhead
Global Balance II
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
If 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(j\right)$
\end_inset

 is steady state probability for state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset

, global balance says
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(j\right)\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}P_{ji}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}P\left(i\right)P_{ij}\]

\end_inset

``the probability of leaving state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset

 should be equal to the probability of arriving in state 
\begin_inset Formula $j$
\end_inset

.''
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
